# yaml-language-server: $schema=https://rangka-os.github.io/rangka-os/schema/0.5/module.json
name: whatsapp
version: 1.0.0
title: {id: WhatsApp ke pelanggan, en: WhatsApp to customers}
summary:
  id: Catatan pesan WhatsApp ke pelanggan (terkirim, dibaca, gagal) dan daftar pelanggan yang tidak mau dikirimi WA.
  en: A log of WhatsApp messages to customers (sent, read, failed) and the list of customers who opted out.
category: sales
icon: send-plane-line
# The shared part of the WhatsApp message types (whatsapp_receipt, whatsapp_reminder, whatsapp_order_ready,
# whatsapp_booking): each of those is its own module, so switching one type on or off is a change set the owner
# approves (config.modules). Messages go out through connector rangka_whatsapp (Rangka Cloud's relay, contract 0063
# §7): the relay checks the opt-out list, the kill switch, the template's approval and the caps before every send,
# and sends a key once. This module keeps what the business sees:
# - whatsapp_message: one row per message a flow asked for, with its status from the relay's events (Terkirim,
#   Sampai, Dibaca, Gagal with the reason, or Tidak dikirim);
# - whatsapp_opt_out: the numbers that must not get a message, from the customer's own BERHENTI (via the relay) or
#   from staff ticking "Tidak mau dikirimi WA" on the customer, which is also sent to the relay.
# Phone numbers are compared in one form, digits with the country code (62812…): customer.wa_number and
# pos_sale.wa_number compute it the same way.
requires: {rangka: '>=0.5', users: ^1.0, contacts: ^1.3}
# the kitchen role writes whatsapp_message when it marks a ticket ready (module whatsapp_order_ready)
optional: {kitchen: ^1.0}
